course: dictionary
lesson: 13103
title: A pole for a flag
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A flagstaff is a tall pole that a flag is flown from. Another word for it is flagpole. Context helps you find the meaning. «Every morning, the children raised the flag to the top of the school flagstaff.» Raised and top tell you the flagstaff is something tall that holds a flag up.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. «The flag flew high on the flagstaff at the castle.» Swap in pole for a flag: «The flag flew high on the pole for a flag at the castle.» It still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Flagstaff can also be a name. Flagstaff is a city in Arizona, USA, and it has a capital letter. A capital letter at the start of a word tells you it is a name of a place, not the pole.
fact: A flagstaff is a tall pole on which a flag is flown.
fact: Flagstaff means the same as flagpole.
fact: Schools, castles, town halls and ships often have flagstaffs.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad Hall has a flagstaff.
fact: The plural of flagstaff can be flagstaffs or flagstaves.
exercise: «The flag was pulled up the flagstaff at nine o'clock.» What is a flagstaff? | *A tall pole for a flag | A small flag | A type of castle wall | A kind of boat
exercise: Which word means the same as flagstaff? | Flagship | Flagstone | *Flagpole | Flagon
exercise: «Astronomers in Flagstaff discovered Pluto in 1930.» Where is Flagstaff? | Australia | London | *Arizona, USA | Scotland
test: «The sailors climbed up to fix the rope on the ship's flagstaff.» Where would you find a flagstaff on a ship? | A flagstaff is a kind of sail | Under the water | *On the ship, as a pole for a flag | In the sea's deep bottom
test: «Toad Hall had a flagstaff at the top of its roof.» What is the flagstaff used for? | *Flying a flag | Keeping birds away | Holding up a tent | Catching fish
exam: Which sentence uses flagstaff correctly? | *The school raised its flag on a tall flagstaff | I walked to the flagstaff and sang a song to my dog | The flagstaff was very hungry and tired | The cat sat on the flagstaff and ate my lunch
